Nadine was almost encouraging it because she wanted closure.

00:29:58.178 --> 00:30:00.000
So I think that was what she thought she thought.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:00.839
It would be on her terms,

00:30:00.920 --> 00:30:01.480
her country,

00:30:01.840 --> 00:30:02.381
her city,

00:30:02.921 --> 00:30:03.981
and he couldn't hurt her.

00:30:04.041 --> 00:30:07.182
She was invincible here and she wasn't.

00:30:10.023 --> 00:30:13.786
Nadine would have felt obligated to meet Al-Mahri.

00:30:14.925 --> 00:30:15.125
One,

00:30:15.486 --> 00:30:22.449
she wanted to make sure that Al-Mahri was not going to dishonour her in terms of sending photos to her parents.

00:30:23.509 --> 00:30:23.970
And two,

00:30:24.849 --> 00:30:29.571
he would be very persuasive and demanding and Nadine would not...

00:30:29.791 --> 00:30:32.394
be the first female,

00:30:32.574 --> 00:30:33.335
particularly,

00:30:33.815 --> 00:30:37.598
who actually gave way to the demands of a stalking,

00:30:38.358 --> 00:30:38.819
jealous,

00:30:38.960 --> 00:30:40.540
controlling individual.

00:30:42.262 --> 00:30:50.549
She probably still felt she could manage the situation by being reasonable because she was a reasonable person.

00:30:51.329 --> 00:30:52.330
It's him that's not.

00:30:55.594 --> 00:30:57.915
We don't have a complete picture of what happened.

00:30:58.175 --> 00:31:00.978
after Al Mahri arrived in the UK on December

00:31:01.538 --> 00:31:03.160
27th, 2014.

00:31:03.599 --> 00:31:05.741
But thanks to her family and CCTV,

00:31:06.241 --> 00:31:09.624
there are glimpses into Nadine's final four days.

00:31:10.305 --> 00:31:12.365
The day after Al Mahri arrived in the UK,

00:31:12.707 --> 00:31:15.107
Nadine cancelled her cinema date with Daniel,

00:31:15.548 --> 00:31:15.888
saying,

00:31:16.269 --> 00:31:16.509
sorry,

00:31:16.588 --> 00:31:18.851
but feeling unwell after the trip to London.

00:31:19.211 --> 00:31:20.731
I won't be able to make it today,

00:31:21.053 --> 00:31:21.512
she said.

00:31:21.913 --> 00:31:23.855
She then followed up with another message.

00:31:24.714 --> 00:31:25.435
To be honest...

00:31:25.635 --> 00:31:28.096
A crazy situation has presented itself.

00:31:28.437 --> 00:31:30.117
It's kind of complicated.

00:31:30.538 --> 00:31:32.960
An ex has turned up on the scene.

00:31:35.020 --> 00:31:35.801
Two days later,

00:31:36.122 --> 00:31:36.241
at

00:31:37.041 --> 00:31:46.027
5.09pm, there is CCTV footage of Al-Mahri leaving Nadine's apartment and then returning a few minutes later.

00:31:47.728 --> 00:31:49.229
About an hour and a half after that,

00:31:49.308 --> 00:31:50.048
Nadine's brother,

00:31:50.269 --> 00:31:50.549
Eamon,

00:31:50.730 --> 00:31:53.290
arrives at the apartment to collect some post.

00:31:59.058 --> 00:32:00.140
As I approached her house,

00:32:01.000 --> 00:32:03.242
I rang the bell and there was some shuffling going on inside.

00:32:04.163 --> 00:32:06.265
So I opened up the letterbox and I could see,

00:32:06.705 --> 00:32:06.965
you know,

00:32:07.026 --> 00:32:07.946
a pair of man's legs.

00:32:07.987 --> 00:32:08.866
They definitely weren't women's,

00:32:08.867 --> 00:32:09.067
you know.

00:32:09.807 --> 00:32:11.128
So I called out through the letterbox,

00:32:12.390 --> 00:32:12.549
saying,

00:32:12.550 --> 00:32:13.111
I can see you,

00:32:13.230 --> 00:32:13.750
open the door,

00:32:13.852 --> 00:32:14.271
who's that?

00:32:15.073 --> 00:32:18.576
And the legs just kind of scuttled off somewhere down the hallway.

00:32:19.916 --> 00:32:20.636
A few minutes later,

00:32:20.676 --> 00:32:21.097
he just said,

00:32:21.157 --> 00:32:21.278
oh,

00:32:21.278 --> 00:32:21.637
is that you,

00:32:21.677 --> 00:32:21.958
Eamon?

00:32:22.439 --> 00:32:23.259
And he opened the door.

00:32:25.020 --> 00:32:28.003
So I was alarmed by this to see him in my sister's flat,

00:32:28.063 --> 00:32:28.943
my sister absent,

00:32:29.304 --> 00:32:29.704
didn't know,

00:32:29.804 --> 00:32:30.064
there's no,

00:32:30.485 --> 00:32:31.586
I don't know how he got in here.

00:32:32.346 --> 00:32:33.047
And then things,

00:32:33.347 --> 00:32:34.928
then we kind of got into a bit of an altercation.

00:32:37.270 --> 00:32:39.052
Shortly after the argument with Eamon,

00:32:39.412 --> 00:32:42.375
Nadine arrived at the flat with her older brother Jamal.

00:32:44.176 --> 00:32:45.417
Protected by her brothers,

00:32:45.737 --> 00:32:48.480
she told Almarie she wanted nothing more to do with him.

00:32:49.140 --> 00:32:52.203
And then Jamal drove him to Cardiff Central Railway Station.

00:32:53.264 --> 00:32:53.564
Here.

00:32:53.783 --> 00:32:56.984
He warned Al-Mahri to stay away from his sister for good.

00:32:58.405 --> 00:33:00.946
But Al-Mahri had no intention of giving up.

00:33:01.866 --> 00:33:04.147
He had more sinister plans in mind.

00:33:05.468 --> 00:33:05.588
At

00:33:06.668 --> 00:33:11.611
7.54pm, Al-Mahri is spotted on CCTV at a local store buying a bottle of gin.

00:33:14.632 --> 00:33:16.233
About a half an hour afterwards,

00:33:16.613 --> 00:33:16.733
at

00:33:17.653 --> 00:33:21.135
8.23pm, he checks into the Futures Inn Hotel in Cardiff Bay.

00:33:23.804 --> 00:33:25.285
Shortly after booking in,

00:33:25.625 --> 00:33:28.405
he goes to the bar and starts drinking tequila.

00:33:30.207 --> 00:33:36.429
Al-Mahri had been violently rebuffed by Nadine's brothers and told where to go,

00:33:36.970 --> 00:33:40.090
which will not have gone down well with a controlling individual.

00:33:40.510 --> 00:33:44.532
This is someone who really wants to assert himself over the situation,

00:33:44.712 --> 00:33:48.034
rather than being sent running by relatives.

00:33:48.594 --> 00:33:51.955
This was a very dangerous bomb waiting to explode.

00:33:54.623 --> 00:33:57.925
Al-Mahri asked the hotel reception to call a mobile number.

00:33:58.505 --> 00:33:59.446
It was Nadine's.

00:34:00.326 --> 00:34:06.630
He told her he'd left his passport and phone at her flat and she needed to bring them to the hotel so he could leave the country.

00:34:07.450 --> 00:34:08.331
She agreed to meet him,

00:34:08.991 --> 00:34:11.333
a decision that would prove fatal.

00:34:13.054 --> 00:34:13.954
This was a kind of,

00:34:14.174 --> 00:34:15.415
you must come back,

00:34:15.755 --> 00:34:17.556
you must come to me.

00:34:18.196 --> 00:34:22.920
This element of control was reaching out again and Nadine really...

00:34:23.523 --> 00:34:24.723
Couldn't argue with that,

00:34:25.063 --> 00:34:27.105
as Al-Mahri wouldn't be able to leave the country.

00:34:33.626 --> 00:34:37.867
She came to the hotel just after nine o'clock and went to Al-Mahri's room,

00:34:38.208 --> 00:34:39.087
number 203.

00:34:49.210 --> 00:34:52.391
He then went out to a nearby restaurant where witnesses reported...

00:34:52.715 --> 00:34:55.820
that things were clearly not that good between the pair.

00:34:58.605 --> 00:34:59.708
They then returned here.

00:35:00.039 --> 00:35:01.340
Around 11 o'clock,

00:35:01.780 --> 00:35:03.983
and for reasons which we simply can't fathom,

00:35:04.282 --> 00:35:06.144
she accompanied him to his room.

00:35:06.824 --> 00:35:08.206
She was never seen alive again.

00:35:24.219 --> 00:35:24.338
No

00:35:24.340 --> 00:35:24.619
Please,

00:35:24.739 --> 00:35:24.980
no

00:35:30.628 --> 00:35:32.710
Two years after they met online,

00:35:33.251 --> 00:35:35.173
and after a campaign of stalking,

00:35:35.814 --> 00:35:37.776
intimidation and blackmail,

00:35:39.878 --> 00:35:42.021
Al-Marri finally killed Nadine.

00:35:47.987 --> 00:35:51.451
He then left her lifeless body in room 203.

00:36:01.623 --> 00:36:02.344
Downstairs,

00:36:02.484 --> 00:36:05.326
Al-Mahri asked the bar manager where he could withdraw

00:36:05.707 --> 00:36:06.807
£10,000.

00:36:15.096 --> 00:36:19.338
Al-Mahri was then caught on CCTV casually walking into a casino.

00:36:21.580 --> 00:36:23.101
He had to register as a member.

00:36:27.935 --> 00:36:33.540
Then he went to the bar where he had three shots of tequila as Nadine's body lay in his hotel room.

00:36:35.783 --> 00:36:39.306
Al-Mahri seemingly didn't care whether he left a trail or not.

00:36:43.410 --> 00:36:44.692
Shortly after 3 a.m.,

00:36:45.031 --> 00:36:47.654
Al-Mahri left his hotel room for the last time,

00:36:48.194 --> 00:36:51.057
placing a Do Not Disturb sign on the handle.

00:36:53.103 --> 00:36:54.565
He asked directions for the M4,

00:36:55.446 --> 00:36:58.669
telling the night porter his sister was still sleeping.

00:37:00.873 --> 00:37:04.696
The final time we see Al-Mahri is him arriving at Heathrow Airport,

00:37:05.077 --> 00:37:07.000
driving Nadine's car at

00:37:08.020 --> 00:37:08.321
7.05am.

00:37:14.155 --> 00:37:17.079
Why did Nadine agree to meet Al Mawry in private?

00:37:17.719 --> 00:37:19.182
I want to find out what Dr.

00:37:19.222 --> 00:37:22.105
Elizabeth Yardley and Mike Berry's thoughts are on this.

00:37:24.548 --> 00:37:25.949
Why did she go back to the hotel room,

00:37:25.990 --> 00:37:26.230
Mike?

00:37:26.791 --> 00:37:29.094
She thinks if she goes back to him,

00:37:29.614 --> 00:37:31.697
he is going to give her that information.

00:37:31.996 --> 00:37:32.557
All the pictures,

00:37:32.697 --> 00:37:33.599
everything she wanted.

00:37:34.755 --> 00:37:34.916
Liz,

00:37:34.916 --> 00:37:37.896
do you think he thought out how he was going to murder her?

00:37:38.597 --> 00:37:40.458
I think he probably had thought about it,

00:37:40.818 --> 00:37:43.358
and that's another thing that we need to be aware of here.

00:37:43.699 --> 00:37:45.719
Murders like this do not happen out of the blue.

00:37:45.739 --> 00:37:47.300
The perpetrator does not snap.

00:37:47.559 --> 00:37:51.880
They don't turn from a normal person one day into a murderer the next.

00:37:52.161 --> 00:37:57.682
This is somebody who had a gradual escalation of controlling and possessive and jealous behaviour.

00:37:58.182 --> 00:37:59.844
This was always a possibility.

00:38:00.307 --> 00:38:01.769
And what he does is interesting.

00:38:01.989 --> 00:38:04.852
He actually kills her in a very personalized way

00:38:05.372 --> 00:38:08.155
Strangling somebody is you have control in your hands.

00:38:08.454 --> 00:38:15.760
You are slowly throttling that person It's a very personal very aggressive very violent way to take somebody's life

00:38:16.201 --> 00:38:25.449
It's inevitable consequence of his controlling behavior ultimately He would meet some resistance and eventually have to enforce his control So if it wasn't Nadine it would be somebody else Mike.

00:38:25.608 --> 00:38:25.729
Yeah,

00:38:25.730 --> 00:38:29.012
but he wouldn't necessarily kill them most cyberstalkers don't kill

00:38:29.271 --> 00:38:30.333
Most stalkers don't kill.

00:38:30.612 --> 00:38:32.735
He had a very high risk of violence,

00:38:33.054 --> 00:38:36.777
which may have resulted in permanent damage to somebody or death.

00:38:38.820 --> 00:38:41.822
I'm in Cardiff investigating the tragic murder of

00:38:42.182 --> 00:38:48.547
28-year-old Nadine Abouris by American Sami Al-Marri on New Year's Eve 2014.

00:38:49.288 --> 00:38:52.871
The pair had met online via an internet dating site.

00:38:54.952 --> 00:38:56.795
The morning after he murdered Nadine,

00:38:56.795 --> 00:38:58.335
he drove to Heathrow Airport.

00:38:58.536 --> 00:39:00.997
and boarded a flight to Qatar in the Middle East.

00:39:01.237 --> 00:39:03.378
He was trying to flee justice.

00:39:03.838 --> 00:39:04.298
Meanwhile,

00:39:04.398 --> 00:39:05.418
back in Cardiff,

00:39:05.739 --> 00:39:11.702
Nadine's body lay undiscovered in his hotel room and Nadine's family had no idea where she was.

00:39:14.782 --> 00:39:15.843
We were texting,

00:39:15.844 --> 00:39:17.023
do you want to meet us uptown,

00:39:17.064 --> 00:39:17.804
what's happened,

00:39:17.864 --> 00:39:18.664
where are you going,

00:39:18.704 --> 00:39:19.385
where have you been,

00:39:19.785 --> 00:39:20.485
what are you doing,

00:39:20.485 --> 00:39:20.766
you know.

00:39:22.326 --> 00:39:25.288
And no response from Nadine was very unusual.

00:39:26.920 --> 00:39:28.420
I was worried and scared.

00:39:29.221 --> 00:39:29.481
Then,

00:39:29.581 --> 00:39:32.884
while Nadine's loved ones were frantically trying to contact her,

00:39:33.704 --> 00:39:35.806
Nadine's body was found.

00:39:36.487 --> 00:39:40.569
The duty manager went into the room and discovered

00:39:41.349 --> 00:39:42.130
Nadine's body.

00:39:42.830 --> 00:39:43.250
The room,

00:39:43.310 --> 00:39:44.092
I understand,

00:39:44.291 --> 00:39:45.472
was dishevelled.

00:39:45.552 --> 00:39:49.355
There were towels all over the floor.

00:39:49.895 --> 00:39:51.116
The drawers had been moved.

00:39:51.436 --> 00:39:55.599
There was bottles everywhere and it looked like some towels had also been stained.

00:39:56.300 --> 00:39:57.800
And from what we heard in court,

00:39:57.941 --> 00:40:06.146
Nadine's body had also been washed and she had been left underneath the bed covers so you could just see her face at the top.

00:40:08.247 --> 00:40:10.429
Soon after Nadine's body was discovered,

00:40:10.889 --> 00:40:13.490
the authorities gave her family the bad news.

00:40:14.231 --> 00:40:17.853
Our brother Jalal came in the door and he had two women with him and

00:40:18.753 --> 00:40:20.695
I just knew that something had happened.

00:40:21.916 --> 00:40:22.416
I just knew.

00:40:23.440 --> 00:40:28.603
And they told her and told us that she was gone and the first thing that we said was he did it.

00:40:31.565 --> 00:40:33.986
I couldn't wish that moment on my worst enemy.

00:40:34.046 --> 00:40:40.350
Sorry,

00:40:40.370 --> 00:40:40.610
sorry.

00:40:45.172 --> 00:40:48.054
Al-Mahri had the money to try to escape justice.

00:40:49.855 --> 00:40:51.616
Soon after he arrived in Qatar,

00:40:51.876 --> 00:40:53.417
Al-Marri boarded another flight,

00:40:53.477 --> 00:40:55.118
this time to Tanzania.

00:40:55.439 --> 00:40:57.960
He was determined to get away with Nadine's murder,

00:40:58.201 --> 00:41:00.122
no matter how much it cost.

00:41:00.422 --> 00:41:01.043
Bizarrely,

00:41:01.383 --> 00:41:02.524
during his time on the run,

00:41:02.784 --> 00:41:05.546
he was in regular phone contact with the police in the UK.

00:41:06.246 --> 00:41:08.388
He told them he was in Thailand.

00:41:09.168 --> 00:41:12.291
This man is not somebody who is thinking straight.

00:41:12.591 --> 00:41:15.753
He probably thought that just a little bit of distance would be enough.

00:41:16.093 --> 00:41:19.836
Sami Al-Marri clearly wanted people to know that Nadine...

00:41:20.576 --> 00:41:24.038
because he rang the hotel several times saying,

00:41:24.078 --> 00:41:25.318
have you found the body yet?

00:41:25.358 --> 00:41:34.262
He also spoke to the police in the hotel and gave them details about what room she was in and the fact that she had died.

00:41:34.322 --> 00:41:40.104
But he also said that she had asked him to help her commit suicide.

00:41:42.785 --> 00:41:47.868
He said that she wanted to die and he was assisting her.

00:41:48.428 --> 00:41:48.668
And he...

00:41:49.004 --> 00:41:52.687
He fabricated this with a suicide note that he'd left on the side,

00:41:52.927 --> 00:41:54.348
some of the words incomprehensible,

00:41:54.489 --> 00:41:56.710
but it was signed from Nadine,

00:41:57.291 --> 00:41:57.811
allegedly.

00:42:00.594 --> 00:42:02.635
An international arrest warrant was applied for,

00:42:03.296 --> 00:42:04.397
and it took some time.

00:42:04.417 --> 00:42:06.578
He was eventually tracked.

00:42:07.099 --> 00:42:09.861
I think the correct expression would be in the bush.

00:42:10.842 --> 00:42:14.985
He was many miles from any known area,

00:42:15.746 --> 00:42:16.386
but in an area,

00:42:16.447 --> 00:42:17.087
I believe,

00:42:17.088 --> 00:42:17.968
in which he had...

00:42:18.460 --> 00:42:19.000
relatives.

00:42:20.681 --> 00:42:22.461
After more than two weeks on the run,

00:42:22.781 --> 00:42:27.042
Al-Marri was arrested and flown back to the UK to face justice.

00:42:28.063 --> 00:42:33.864
It was only during the post-mortem that the true horror of what happened to Nadine was revealed.

00:42:37.565 --> 00:42:40.426
The coroner's report found that Nadine's body was covered in

00:42:40.786 --> 00:42:41.847
17 bruises,

00:42:41.967 --> 00:42:43.327
marks and abrasions,

00:42:43.587 --> 00:42:45.348
including a bite to her forearm.

00:42:51.924 --> 00:42:54.566
This was somebody completely out of control.

00:42:55.226 --> 00:42:56.968
Going back to what we know about him,

00:42:58.288 --> 00:42:59.569
he's got a chaotic life.

00:43:00.690 --> 00:43:03.552
And now he's committed murder in a very chaotic fashion.

00:43:04.533 --> 00:43:05.734
He could have just strangled her,

00:43:05.754 --> 00:43:06.314
but he didn't.

00:43:06.454 --> 00:43:07.535
There were the bite marks,

00:43:07.555 --> 00:43:08.355
there were scratches.

00:43:08.796 --> 00:43:09.536
And without a doubt,

00:43:09.556 --> 00:43:10.737
she fought back.

00:43:11.437 --> 00:43:15.620
But he just wanted to physically hurt her so people could see her like that.

00:43:17.922 --> 00:43:19.523
He had no feelings for her,

00:43:19.883 --> 00:43:20.804
no empathy for her.

00:43:21.128 --> 00:43:21.848
It shows that

00:43:22.629 --> 00:43:24.270
Aria of being a sociopathic predator.

00:43:28.472 --> 00:43:33.875
Sami Al-Mahri was tried at Cardiff Crown Court in November 2016.

00:43:34.996 --> 00:43:35.456
Initially,

00:43:36.016 --> 00:43:39.818
he only admitted to manslaughter on the grounds of diminished responsibility.

00:43:40.599 --> 00:43:42.140
But on the second day of his trial,

00:43:42.620 --> 00:43:44.761
he suddenly changed his plea to murder.

00:43:45.582 --> 00:43:49.704
Al-Mahri claimed he was suffering from an abnormality of mental function.

00:43:50.004 --> 00:43:53.546
and said that he heard the voice of God telling him to kill Nadine Abouris.

00:43:53.946 --> 00:43:56.488
The judge gave him a life sentence for murder.

00:43:58.469 --> 00:43:58.869
Clearly,

00:43:58.929 --> 00:44:03.812
he decided he no longer wished to put forward what we had always said was a false defence.

00:44:05.113 --> 00:44:13.818
Al-Marri was a dangerous and obsessive man who used social media to conduct a two-year relationship with Nadine before brutally murdering her.

00:44:14.658 --> 00:44:15.759
Without social media,

00:44:16.179 --> 00:44:17.960
would Nadine still be alive today?

00:44:18.740 --> 00:44:19.821
I want to hear what Dr.

00:44:19.861 --> 00:44:23.443
Elizabeth Yardley and clinical forensic psychologist Mike Berry think.

00:44:24.763 --> 00:44:24.923
Liz,

00:44:25.324 --> 00:44:27.725
what kind of murderer was Al-Ma'ri?

00:44:28.405 --> 00:44:28.565
Well,

00:44:28.566 --> 00:44:33.368
Al-Ma'ri was a predator because social media allowed him access to his victim.

00:44:33.928 --> 00:44:38.571
Social media was all the way through this dynamic between these two people,

00:44:38.931 --> 00:44:42.953
so he used it to monitor and control his victim as well,

00:44:43.013 --> 00:44:44.794
so it wasn't just used to find her,

00:44:45.114 --> 00:44:47.996
it was an integral part all the way through of this relationship.

00:44:48.620 --> 00:44:51.401
A really important tool in his toolbox of control.

00:44:52.181 --> 00:44:52.401
Mike,

00:44:52.421 --> 00:44:55.682
what are the red flags that you would suggest that people look out for online?

00:44:56.102 --> 00:44:59.203
If they've made claims of being world champion boxer,

00:44:59.243 --> 00:45:00.404
world champion this and this,

00:45:00.804 --> 00:45:01.784
check it out.

00:45:02.284 --> 00:45:04.605
Use the internet to find out about them.

00:45:05.085 --> 00:45:05.405
Also,

00:45:06.145 --> 00:45:07.246
if they're on Facebook,

00:45:07.646 --> 00:45:10.227
look at their Facebook connections,

00:45:10.228 --> 00:45:11.007
things like that.

00:45:11.527 --> 00:45:14.028
Do a bit of homework before you fall in love with a guy.

00:45:14.684 --> 00:45:14.865
Liz,

00:45:14.965 --> 00:45:18.551
what needs to be done and what could be done online to protect someone like Nadine?

00:45:18.912 --> 00:45:19.032
Well,

00:45:19.072 --> 00:45:23.420
I think first and foremost we need to raise awareness of this kind of behaviour.

00:45:23.660 --> 00:45:26.903
Because it is something that is getting all too common now.

00:45:26.963 --> 00:45:29.845
We see abusers using social media,

00:45:30.005 --> 00:45:36.251
using technology as a way of meeting victims and as a way of controlling them once they've got them under their spell.

00:45:38.052 --> 00:45:39.213
Without social media,

00:45:39.633 --> 00:45:42.676
there can be little doubt that Nadine would still be alive today.

00:45:43.917 --> 00:45:46.539
Our life now will never be the same.

00:45:47.340 --> 00:45:49.722
We have to take comfort in each other,

00:45:49.762 --> 00:45:52.344
but that's a very difficult thing to do.

00:45:53.140 --> 00:45:53.901
We're scattered,

00:45:54.501 --> 00:45:55.802
we're still grieving,

00:45:55.922 --> 00:45:56.963
we're still sad,

00:45:57.043 --> 00:46:01.567
and we're still blaming each other internally about what we could have done.

00:46:02.207 --> 00:46:03.608
How could this ever be stopped?

00:46:05.129 --> 00:46:05.690
And I hope,

00:46:07.491 --> 00:46:17.419
I hope that there will be some warnings to others that it won't always end up as happily married forever.

